    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests passing).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `locality` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner response, computed from `city` via the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else UNKNOWN). Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that derives `locality` from `owner.getCity()` as an inline expression, alongside the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\nThe derivation lives in the mapper because that's where every other read-only derived owner field is computed, and it flows out through the existing `RespondWithOwner` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` responders unchanged.\n\n## One subtlety worth noting\n\nMy first attempt put the lookup in a `default String localityOf(String city)` helper method on the mapper interface. That broke unrelated tests with a 500: MapStruct scans the interface for candidate mapping methods, saw a `String\u2192String` method, and started applying it to *every* String property in `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` \u2014 corrupting the telephone (among others) so the normalized E.164 value never reached persistence and tripped the entity's `@Pattern` constraint. Inlining the logic as a pure expression (the same style the other derived fields use) avoids introducing any method MapStruct could mistake for a converter.",
